        "content": "Welcome to **Oxygen Not Included**! You’ve spawned in a cold biome (likely the Rime asteroid or a Frosty DLC start), which adds a unique challenge: keeping things warm enough to grow food, while most of your water is currently frozen.\n\nHere is exactly what you should do in the first 2-3 cycles:\n\n### 1. Dig Out Your Living Space\nFirst, use the **Dig (G)** tool. You want to create horizontal \"floors\" that are 4 tiles high. \n*   **Where:** Dig out to the left and right of your Printing Pod. This pod provides a little bit of light and a tiny bit of oxygen to start.\n*   **Goal:** Create flat areas for your first rooms.\n\n### 2. Sanitation (The Most Urgent Task)\nIf you don't build toilets, your Duplicants will make a mess on the floor, which leads to germs and stress.\n*   **Where:** Dig a room a bit to the side (maybe to the right of the pod).\n*   **What to build:** Go to the **Plumbing** tab and build **2 Outhouses** and **1 Wash Basin**. \n*   **Pro-Tip:** Make sure the Wash Basin is set to \"Direction: Left\" (or whichever way they exit) so they are forced to wash their hands after using the toilet.\n\n### 3. Oxygen\nYou have some oxygen in the air now, but it will run out fast.\n*   **What to build:** In the **Oxygen** tab, build an **Algae Deoxidizer** near your pod. \n*   **Power:** You’ll need a **Manual Generator** (hamster wheel) and a **Tiny Battery** (under the **Power** tab) connected with wires to make it run.\n\n### 4. Sleeping\n*   **What to build:** In the **Furniture** tab, build **3 Cots** (one for each Duplicant).\n*   **Where:** Place them together in a room to create a \"Barracks,\" which gives them a morale boost.\n\n### 5. Find Liquid Water\nLooking at your screenshot, that big blue area below you is mostly **Ice**. You can't pump ice!\n*   **Where to look:** Look at the first image, the green area at the very top has a pool of **Liquid Water**. \n*   **Action:** Dig a path upward toward that green biome. Once you reach the water, build a **Pitcher Pump** (Plumbing tab) over it. Your Duplicants need this liquid water to fill the Wash Basin so they stay clean.\n\n### 6. Food (The Cold Problem)\nYou start with some rations (16,000 kcal), but you’ll need more.\n*   **Short term:** Dig into any tiles that have \"cracks\" in them (Buried Objects). These often contain **Muckroot**, which is free food.\n*   **Long term:** Since you are in a cold area, normal plants like Mealwood might not grow because it's too chilly. Look for **Hexalent** fruit in the surroundings for now while you research heaters.\n\n**Summary of your first dig path:**\n1.  Dig **Right** for a Bathroom.\n2.  Dig **Left** for a Bedroom.\n3.  Dig **Up** to reach that liquid water pool in the green area.\n\nGood luck, and try not to let them hold it in for too long!",
